 "text": "CITY OF MANILA\nAGENCY ACTION PLAN AND STATUS of IMPLEMENTATION\nAudit Observations and Recommendations\nFor the Calendar Year 2024\nAs of August 31, 2025\nAction Plan\nAGENCY ACTION PLAN\nPerson/Dept.\nResponsible\nTarget Implementation Date\nStatus of\nImplementation\nFrom\nTo\nReference\nAAR 2024\nObservation No. 4\nPage 92\nc.\nAudit Observations\nMisclassified tax credits amounting to P510.615\nmillion in the Other Receivables - Others account and\nunrecorded Other Receivables amounting to\nP770.569 million; and\nd.\nUnreconciled balance of P9.309 million due to\nnon-recording of cleared dishonored checks under\nthe Other Receivables - Dishonored Checks account.\nThese are contrary to Paragraph 27 of the IPSAS 1;\nSections 111 and 112 of PD\nNo. 1445; and\nItems 6.1 and 6,2 of COA Circular No. 2016-005, dated\nDecember 19, 2016.\n4. The balance of the RPT and Special Education Tax\n(SET) Receivable amounting to P15.773 billion and\nP10.885 billion, respectively, as of December 31,\n2024, cannot be ascertained due to the following:\na.The RPT and SET Receivables per books do not\nAudit Recommendations\nConduct a regular review and reconciliation of\nreceivables, including monthly or quarterly\nreporting, to ensure the accuracy of balances in\nthe financial statements; and\nCoordinate and reconcile with the Patrimonial\nUnit of the City General Services Office's (CGSO)\nto establish the correct balances for the leased\nproperties of the City\nb.The MUSO to:\nSubmit a complete and up-to-date schedule of\nreceivables, including collections and ageing\nreports pertaining to the Land for the Landless\nprogram, to OCAT on a timely basis.\n4.19.We recommended and Management\nagreed and acted upon on the recommendations\nto:\na. Require the CTO to provide the OCAT with\nRPTODL for monitoring purposes;\nb.Direct the OCAT and the CTO to coordinate\nand reconcile discrepancies between recorded\nbalances of RPT and SET Receivable accounts\nagainst the total amount of tax delinquencies\nindicated in the RPTODL;\nc. Direct the OCAT to make a reliable estimate of\ntally with the total RPT Delinquencies recorded in the the City's bad debts arising from uncollected\nReal Property Tax Owners Delinquency Listing\n(RPTODL) by P1.207 billion, due to non-coordination\nbetween the OCAT and CTO, which resulted in\nunreconciled data, contrary to Paragraph 27 of\nIPSAS 1; and\ntaxes and set up an allowance for impairment\nbased on the most reliable and available data that\nthe OCAT can obtain; '\nThe OCAT will reconcile the discrepancies\nand will coordinate closely with the CTO\nfor review, analysis and reconciliation of\nthese accounts. They also committed to\nundertake a comprehensive assessment\nof uncollected tax accounts\nPage 3 of 24\nMUSO\nСТО, ОСАТ\nReason for Partial/Delay/\nNon-Implementation, if\napplicable\nAction Taken/Action to\nbe Taken\n",
